    "extract": "Old Heidelberg is a 1959 West German historical drama film directed by Ernst Marischka and starring Christian Wolff, Gert Fröbe and Sabine Sinjen. It is an adaptation of the 1901 play Old Heidelberg by Wilhelm Meyer-Förster. It was shot at the Spandau Studios in Berlin with sets designed by the art directors Hertha Hareiter and Otto Pischinger.",
    "extract_html": "<p><i><b>Old Heidelberg</b></i> is a 1959 West German historical drama film directed by Ernst Marischka and starring Christian Wolff, Gert Fröbe and Sabine Sinjen. It is an adaptation of the 1901 play <i>Old Heidelberg</i> by Wilhelm Meyer-Förster. It was shot at the Spandau Studios in Berlin with sets designed by the art directors Hertha Hareiter and Otto Pischinger.</p>"
